-- title:
--   Flat-local description of fibres of the level-ℓ fine uniformisation
-- statement:
--   The setting is the following. Fixed are natural numbers $r$, $\bar r$, $N$ with $r$ and $\bar r$ prime, $N$ nonzero, $\bar r\neq r$, neither $r$ nor $\bar r$ dividing $N$, and $N$ squarefree.
--
--   *Coefficient rings.* $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), with an irreducible element $\pi$, complete for the $\pi$-adic topology, residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`), and with $(r)=(\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero field which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a characteristic-zero domain, an $\mathcal O$-algebra, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, such that $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}$ modulo $\pi$ for all $x$ (`hFr`). Further, $\mathrm{vdet}\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) is a homomorphism with $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\,\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   *Indefinite quaternion data and moduli.* $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is indefinite and ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$ in the sense of `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`: $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ every nonzero element of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a unit precisely when $v$ contains $r$ or $\bar r$; $\Lambda$ is a maximal order in it. The scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with its point assignment $\mathrm{pt}$ is a coarse moduli space for `FakeEllipticCurve Λ N` (isomorphism invariance, compatibility with base change, surjectivity and injectivity on geometric points, and the universal property), and its generic fibre, the projection of the fibre product of $f$ with $\operatorname{Spec} K_0$, is geometrically reduced and geometrically connected. An integer $n\ge 3$ is coprime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$; $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with $\mathrm{ptF}$ is a fine moduli space for fake elliptic curves with full level-$n$ structure (`hM`), and $\rho\colon G\to\operatorname{Aut} M$, $\chi\colon G\to\Lambda$ constitute a level-twist action (`hρ`: $\rho$ acts over the base, transports level structures twisted by $\chi(g)$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, injective and surjective modulo $n$). A morphism $p\colon M\to\mathcal X$ lies over the base (`hp`), is invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`), and carries the level-$n$ moduli points to the coarse moduli points (`hp_pt`).
--
--   *Hecke tower and Atkin–Lehner data.* For each prime $\ell$ different from $r$ and $\bar r$, $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with $\mathrm{ptT}_\ell$ is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with extra level $\ell$ (`h𝒴`), and $d_0(\ell), d_1(\ell)\colon\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ lie over the base and satisfy: $d_0$ forgets the extra level (`hd₀`), while $d_1$ sends a point with extra level $\ell$ to the target of any $\ell$-level isogeny out of it (`hd₁`). The endomorphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ lie over the base and realise the Atkin–Lehner quotient relation at $r$, respectively $\bar r$, on moduli points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   *Definite quaternion data.* $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ ($a_1<0$, $b_1<0$, and division at $v$ exactly for $v\ni\bar r$); $\Lambda_1$ is a maximal order, $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$), $R_1\le\Lambda_1$; $n_1$ is a unit of the finite adelic algebra lying in the $r$-Hecke set of $R_1$ (it lies in the finite adelic box of $R_1$, as does $r\,n_1^{-1}$, while $n_1^{-1}$ and $r^{-1}n_1$ do not), and the intersection $R_1\cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ is an Eichler order of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); $\iota_0$ is an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$; $v$ is a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $r$. The subgroup $\tilde\Gamma$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ is characterised elementwise (`hΓt`) as [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraphAtPrime.html#L37), the intersection over all places $w\neq v$ of the preimages, under the local inclusions, of the subgroups generated by the local box units of $R_1$ at $w$. For each tower prime $\ell$ there are given $s(\ell)\in\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ and an adelic unit $sf(\ell)$ such that (`hs`) $sf(\ell)$ has component $s(\ell)\otimes 1$ at every place not containing $r$ and component $1$ at places containing $r$, the product of the central idele of $\ell$ with $sf(\ell)^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` if $\ell\mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s(\ell))=\ell$; and $\tilde\Gamma(\ell)=\tilde\Gamma\cap s(\ell)\tilde\Gamma s(\ell)^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). An element $\bar w$ has reduced norm $\bar r$ and normalises $\tilde\Gamma$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   *Uniformisation families.* $\theta_t\colon\tilde\Gamma\to G$ is a group homomorphism. On $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, $\Theta_f$ assigns to a triple consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$, a Deligne datum in $\Omega_{K_0,\pi}(B)$ and an element of $G$ a $B$-point of $M$ over $\mathcal O$; it is natural in $B$ (`hnat`), satisfies $\rho(h)$-equivariance in the form $\rho(h)_*\Theta_f(x,gh)=\Theta_f(x,g)$ (`hG`), is invariant under the twisted action of $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma$, namely $\Theta_f(x',\theta_t(\gamma)g)=\Theta_f(x,g)$ whenever $x'$ is obtained from $x$ by `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` for $\iota_0(\gamma)$, that is the coefficient map of $x'$ is the $\mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0\gamma)}$-twist of that of $x$ and the Deligne datum of $x'$ is the pullback of that of $x$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$ (`hinv`), and is formally étale (`het`): for a surjection $p\colon B\to B_0$ of $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebras whose kernel has vanishing products, every $B$-point of $M$ lifting $\Theta_f(x_0)$ comes from a unique lift of $x_0$. For each tower prime there is also given a family $\Theta_T(\ell)$ with values in the $B$-points of $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\mathcal O$, taking as argument a pair consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ and a Deligne datum.
--
--   *Level-$\ell$ data.* Finally $\ell$ is a fixed prime different from $r$ and $\bar r$, $M_\ell$ is a scheme over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with structure morphism $f_{M_\ell}$ locally of finite type (`hfMℓ`), and $\Theta_{f,\ell}$ is a family of the same shape as $\Theta_f$ with values in the $B$-points of $M_\ell$, satisfying naturality (`hnatℓ`), the twisted invariance restricted to $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma$ with $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma(\ell)$ (`hinvℓ`), formal étaleness (`hetℓ`), and the following description of geometric fibres (`hfibℓ`): for an algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent, for $\psi,\psi'\colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to k$, Deligne data $P,P'$ over $k$ and $g,g'\in G$, one has $\Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi,P),g)=\Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi',P'),g')$ if and only if there is $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma$ with $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma(\ell)$ such that $g'=\theta_t(\gamma)g$, $P'$ is the pullback of $P$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$ in the sense of `DeligneDatum.IsPullback`, and $\psi'(y)=\mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0\gamma)}$-twist of $\psi$ at $y$ for every $y\in O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ fixed by $\mathrm{Fr}^{\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0 z)}$ for all central $z\in\tilde\Gamma$ (those with $z=c\cdot 1$ for some $c\in\mathbb Q$) with $\theta_t(z)=1$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, all $x_1,x_2$ consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ together with a Deligne datum over $B$, and all $g_1,g_2\in G$ with $\Theta_{f,\ell}(x_1,g_1)=\Theta_{f,\ell}(x_2,g_2)$, there exist a natural number $k$, commutative rings $B'_1,\dots,B'_k$, each an $\mathcal O$-algebra and a $B$-algebra compatibly (scalar tower over $\mathcal O$), each flat as a $B$-module, such that every prime of $B$ is the contraction of a prime of some $B'_i$ (`hcov`), and elements $\gamma_1,\dots,\gamma_k$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ with $\gamma_i\in\tilde\Gamma$ and $\gamma_i\in\tilde\Gamma(\ell)$, for which the following three assertions hold for every $i$.
--
--   First, over $B'_i$ the Deligne datum obtained from $x_2$ by base change is the pullback along $\iota_0(\gamma_i)^{-1}$ of the Deligne datum obtained from $x_1$ by base change, in the sense of `DeligneDatum.IsPullback`.
--
--   Second, for every $y\in O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ that is fixed by $\mathrm{Fr}^{\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0 z)}$ for all $z\in\tilde\Gamma$ which are rational scalars and satisfy $\theta_t(z)=1$, the coefficient map $O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B'_i$ obtained from $x_2$ by base change sends $y$ to the value at $y$ of the $\mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0\gamma_i)}$-twist (`frobTwist`) of the coefficient map obtained from $x_1$ by base change.
--
--   Third, $g_2=\theta_t(\gamma_i)\,g_1$ in $G$.
--
--   This is a step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld $r$-adic uniformisation of the Shimura curve attached to an indefinite quaternion algebra ramified at $r$ and $\bar r$, at the level of the fine moduli problem with an extra level-$\ell$ structure: it converts the description of the geometric fibres of $\Theta_{f,\ell}$ as orbits of $\tilde\Gamma\cap\tilde\Gamma(\ell)$ into a statement over an arbitrary $\pi$-nilpotent base, after passage to a finite flat family of algebras covering $\operatorname{Spec} B$. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuliT.existsUnique_factor_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_fine`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuliT.existsUnique_factor_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_fine).
